 "note": "From an autosave. Since the Jamāʿa of 2 September 1448, called by the two princes, the commons sit in the Jamāʿa as an equal estate (the privilege 'peasants represented in parliament'); their satisfaction has risen from 50 to 59, the burghers' from 54 to 56. Stability is 17.7, the highest in years. The army of al-Andalus landed on Sardinia in September and destroyed Arborea's army at Seddori (26 September); Yūsuf sank five Genoese ships in the Corsica Channel (21 October). The fleet has grown from 9 war galleys to 22, with 10 hulks: 87 ships. On 5 November al-Andalus joined the Mamlūks' war on the Banū Lām. In the ṭāʾifas, the king of al-Burtughāl died at sea (1 June 1448) and his widow rules as regent for their daughter; Maryam, Shaykha of Qūnka, died (28 June) and her son succeeded her. Treasury 219. Estate power estimated from the reading of 16 November 1428.",
